description:
Objective: decide, in writing, whether same-user host processes stay outside the protected profile's threat model. Two open points depend on it:
- CQ-R01 follow-up 5: daemon.json's port↔pid binding is not portably verifiable.
- CQ-R08's handoff on CQ-R13, point 3: the per-request daemon.json re-check before a forward has a theoretical TOCTOU window.

Created by architect-e4b7eee0 on 2026-10-30, when the human moved the non-gating R01 follow-ups out of CQ-R13. This is a spike: its deliverable is a decision, not code.

Deliverable: one decision document under docs/, linked from docs/ARCHITECTURE.md's security notes. It contains:
- the threat-model statement;
- both open points, with references to the code (readDaemonInfo, the guest-session forward path);
- the options considered, each with its reason:
  - a per-platform OS lookup of the port's owner;
  - a daemon-issued nonce over /health;
  - accepting and documenting the gap;
- the decision;
- the follow-up rows to create, if the decision changes behavior.

Out of scope:
- implementing any option;
- .moe edits.

Verification command (fresh, exit 0 required): npm run lint (repo root), and the decision document exists with those sections.

implementationPlan.note:
Created docs/design/protected-profile-threat-model.md with the six H2 headings in order. The decision is as planned. The record runs 197 lines, against the plan's "about 170", because it documents three facts step 1 surfaced:
(1) task-801272c4's Origin rule has landed, so it is described as landed;
(2) the pid-guess redirect refinement under open point 1, plus the runner key going to the file's port;
(3) /health has no Host check (DNS rebinding). I filed this as new row task-80930ce6 (LOW, BACKLOG, this epic) and named it in Follow-up rows as required by decision 2.
Decision 3 is scoped to the live daemon's identity, bind and reachability, so it does not overclaim against the profile read (RF02's area) or agentCommand. Everything is at the problem-class level, with no walkthrough.

docs/ARCHITECTURE.md had no changes before the edit (git status --short printed nothing). I inserted `## Security Notes` immediately before `## Error Handling (Current)`, following the file's pattern of bullets, a blank line, `---` and a blank line. It has three bullets:
1. the link to design/protected-profile-threat-model.md, with what is inside and outside the model and the single-user-host assumption;
2. the refusal-not-admission rule for the live daemon;
3. the accepted gaps.
It carries no task ids. The diff is 14 insertions, no other line changed, and git diff --check is clean.
